<title>GERMANY: Germany to allow arbitration on public works.</title>
<headline>Germany to allow arbitration on public works.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>In a move aimed at averting U.S. trade sanctions, Germany will allow bidders on public works projects to seek arbitration in contested cases, economics minister Guenter Rexrodt said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Chancellor Helmut Kohl's cabinet decided on the move at a meeting on Wednesday, just ahead of a September 30 deadline set by the U.S. Trade Representative's Office in response to complaints brought by General Electric Co and Westinghouse Electric Corp.</p>
<p>Rexrodt said he hoped the decision would lead to an easing of tensions with the U.S.</p>
<p>In future, companies that feel disadvantaged in the bidding process will have recourse to the German courts.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
